<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ly Nam De</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">503–548</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Lý Nam Đế, Ly Bi, Lý Bí</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ly Nam De, born Ly Bi, led a rising against the Liang dynasty's rule of Jiaozhou in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. By 544 he had expelled the Liang officials and proclaimed himself emperor of the south, naming his state Van Xuan and founding the Early Ly dynasty. Liang forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-chen">Chen Baxian</a> defeated him in 545, and he died in 548.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ly-nam-de.jpg" alt="Ly Nam De" width="320" height="543" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Ly_Nam_De.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
